# armour/man/padded_hang: the gambeson's short quilted skirt on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 27.2: T1's skirt is
# short): one stuffed row bulging past the seam, lit at the top-left, its hem a closed outline; it opens over the stride
# (wide) and trails in the run (flare). Finish regions: R the hem row, W a 2-pixel fray mark on the shadow side.
# Keys: the hang channel in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) the quilt softened: the lit side's seam rows a step up (8/7, not 8/6), so the T1 coat reads as stuffed
# cloth and not as bandage stripes; the shadow side keeps its flat step 1.
use person
body man
role armour padded
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
z 10
# (ladder i2, integration) the quilt in undyed buff (cloth3), not the tunic's cloth1: a gambeson over a same-colour
# tunic read as the bare tunic at 1x (C4 12 %); the T1 coat now reads as a coat
legend 5 cloth3 0
legend 6 cloth3 1
legend 7 cloth3 2
legend 8 cloth3 3
legend 9 cloth3 4

